dma-buf: dma_buf_fd() does not take a reference on a file that is being freed

Audit finding D4. The dma-buf and its file have separate counts here (in linux
dma_buf_put() is fput()). The last fput() of the file on one cpu drops f_count to zero and
only then takes db->lock to clear db->file; an export of the same buffer on another cpu
in that window found db->file, raised the count from zero and installed a descriptor on a
file that was freed a moment later (use after free; with the last reference dropped from
the poll work item, a second release and a double free of the buffer). The reference is
now taken only if the count is not zero; otherwise a new file is made, and the old file's
release, which checks db->file == filp, leaves it alone.

--- a/src/Kernel/fbsdkpi/drm/src/sf_dma_buf.c
+++ b/src/Kernel/fbsdkpi/drm/src/sf_dma_buf.c
@@ -151,9 +151,12 @@
 		return fd;
 	mutex_lock(&db->lock);
 	filp = db->file;
-	if (filp != NULL) {
+	// a file whose last reference is being dropped on another cpu is still db->file until
+	// its release takes db->lock: taking a reference on it then would hand out a
+	// descriptor to a file that is freed a moment later. such a file counts as absent,
+	// and its release leaves the new db->file alone.
+	if (filp != NULL && refcount_acquire_if_not_zero(&filp->f_count)) {
 		// the existing file already holds a buffer reference
-		refcount_acquire(&filp->f_count);
 		mutex_unlock(&db->lock);
 		dma_buf_put(db);
 	} else {

